The Company is a Maryland corporation organized in March 2019 and operates principally through its wholly-owned subsidiary, Pioneer Bank, National Association (the “Bank”). The Bank was first chartered in 1889 as a New York state chartered savings bank and following approval by the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency (the “OCC”) converted to a national bank on April 1, 2024. On July 17, 2019, the Company became the holding company for the Bank, when it closed its stock offering in connection with the completion of the reorganization of the Bank into the two-tier mutual holding company form of organization. The Company’s common stock is traded on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol “PBFS.”

